{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","reason":"Add shared run_auto_maintenance(tracker): explicit git maintenance run --auto bounded by watchdog-grade _LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT, decoupled from the per-commit latency bound; and the automaint-off config tuple."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py","reason":"Suppress git auto-maintenance on the lock-held write commit (_git_commit/_git_commit_paths) so the 30s _GIT_TIMEOUT covers only the commit, not an O(store) foreground repack."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","reason":"After a successful lock-held commit, run explicit auto-maintenance under the same write lock (ADR 0051 serialization preserved) so loose-object growth is still bounded. ALSO: Cover the two recovery-path lock-held commits that build their own argv (_recover_from_unmerged, _recover_from_invalid_object) by injecting _AUTOMAINT_OFF; plus the post-commit deferred run_auto_maintenance under the write lock."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/txn.py","reason":"Parity: the claim/transition write commit is the sibling lock-held commit surface; apply the same maint-suppression + explicit post-commit maintenance."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py","reason":"RED->GREEN regression: a write whose foreground auto-maintenance would exceed the commit timeout must still succeed (write not lost), with _GIT_TIMEOUT unchanged at 30s."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/delete.py","reason":"Suppress-only: inject _AUTOMAINT_OFF on the DELETE + UNLINK-cleanup commits (run_git_write, 120s). delete.py holds NO store write lock, so no deferred maintenance here; loose objects are repacked by the next locked write."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py","reason":"Suppress-only: inject _AUTOMAINT_OFF on commit_ticket_dir. compact IS the store-maintenance/fold path, so no unserialized deferred maintenance here."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store_batch_write.py","reason":"Adjust test-internal subprocess fakes: detect the commit regardless of leading -c config flags (argv shape changed)."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store_delete_events.py","reason":"Adjust test-internal subprocess fake: detect commit regardless of leading -c flags."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store_write_index_reset_on_failure.py","reason":"Adjust test-internal subprocess fakes: detect commit regardless of leading -c flags."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py","reason":"Adjust test-internal subprocess fake: count commits regardless of leading -c flags."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"Suppress-only: inject _AUTOMAINT_OFF on the ticket-compact-all backfill commit (lock-held snapshot-compaction commit). Like compact_plan.py this IS the maintenance/fold path, so no unserialized deferred maintenance here."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py","reason":"Suppress-only: inject _AUTOMAINT_OFF on the a3-remediation batch commits (lock-held, one commit per 200-ticket batch). Prevents an O(store) foreground repack from being charged to a batch commit; loose objects are repacked by the next locked write's deferred maintenance."}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787963319021642001,"uuid":"0a2170ea-b80d-4d20-ac74-a05f69e4b821"}